ial protein grown on natural gas as feed for pigs</article-title><source>Acta Agr Scand A-AN</source><year>2001</year><volume>51</volume><fpage>97</fpage><lpage>106</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hellwing</surname><given-names>ALF</given-names></name><name><surname>Tauson</surname><given-names>A-H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kjos</surname><given-names>NP</given-names></name><name><surname>Skrede</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bacterial protein meal in diets for growing pigs &#x02013; effects on protein and energy metabolism</article-title><source>Animal</source><year>2007</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>45</fpage><lpage>54</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1017/S1751731107283879</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hellwing</surname><given-names>ALF</given-names></name><name><surname>Tauson</surname><given-names>A-H</given-names></name><name><surname>Skrede</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kjos</surname><given-names>NP</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahlstr&#x000f8;m </surname><given-names>&#x000d8;</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bacterial protein meal in diets for pigs and minks - Comparative studies on protein turnover rate and urinary excretion of purine base derivatives</article-title><source>Arch Anim Nutr </source><year>2007</year><volume>61</volume><fpage>425</fpage><lpage>43</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18069615</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/17450390701565248</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Clifford</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Story</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Levels of purines in foods a